The '''2027 Los Angeles Dodgers season''' will be the 138th season for the [[Los Angeles Dodgers]] franchise in [[Major League Baseball]] (MLB), their 70th season in [[Los Angeles]], [[California]], and their 66th season playing home games at [[Dodger Stadium]]. The Dodgers will seek to make their fifteenth straight playoff appearance, which would surpass the 1991–2005 [[Atlanta Braves]] as the longest consecutive postseason streak in MLB history. They will also attempt to secure their sixth straight [[National League West]] title and make a return to the World Series after a one-year absence.<ref>{{cite news |title=Longest streaks of consecutive playoff appearances in MLB history |first=Cole |last=Jacobson |website=MLB.com |date=September 14, 2026 |access-date=October 15, 2026 |url=https://www.mlb.com/news/most-consecutive-playoff-seasons-in-mlb-history}}</ref>

== Offseason ==
=== Roster departures ===
On October 29, 2026, the day after the conclusion of the [[2026 World Series]], nine Dodgers players became free agents. This included left-handed pitchers [[Tarik Skubal]], [[Alex Vesia]], [[Kris Bubic]], and [[Eric Lauer]]; right-handed pitchers [[Evan Phillips]], [[Blake Treinen]], and [[Brusdar Graterol]]; and utility players [[Miguel Rojas (baseball)|Miguel Rojas]] and [[Enrique Hernández (baseball)|Kiké Hernández]].<ref name=FreeAgents>{{cite news |title=Dodgers 2026 Offseason Guide on Free Agents, Trade Targets, More Roster Shakeups After NLCS Sweep |first=Kerry |last=Miller |website=Bleacher Report |date=October 15, 2026 |access-date=October 15, 2026 |url=https://bleacherreport.com/articles/25505146-dodgers-2026-offseason-guide-free-agents-trade-targets-more-roster-shakeups-after-nlcs-sweep}}</ref> Rojas, who initially announced his intention to retire at the end of the previous season, confirmed his retirement on October 15.<ref>{{cite news |title=Miguel Rojas teases delaying retirement one more year, but Dodgers can’t bite |first=Matthew |last=Swigonski |website=Dodgers Way |date=October 3, 2026 |access-date=October 15, 2026 |url=https://dodgersway.com/miguel-rojas-teases-delaying-retirement-one-more-year-dodgers-cant-bite}}</ref><ref name=Rojas>{{cite news |title=Dodgers Veteran Announces Immediate Retirement After NLCS Loss to Brewers |first=Noah |last=Camras |work=Sports Illustrated |date=October 15, 2026 |access-date=October 15, 2026 |url=https://www.si.com/mlb/dodgers/onsi/dodgers-veteran-announces-immediate-retirement-after-nlcs-loss-brewers}}</ref>

